// Decorations: themed deco blocks that dress POIs and that players unlock and build with. As in
// Empyrion, a deco piece is a block in the shared block catalogue, grouped into families (here,
// theme sets) that each furnish one kind of room. The broken, burnt, overgrown and knocked-over
// states are POI and Creative blocks; only the intact piece is built in survival.
//
// palettes   colour per slot (rrggbb). "base" has every slot; a set's palette overrides some.
//            Slots: body trim dark metal chrome wood fabric linen paper plastic glass screen lamp
//            signal plant soil stone bronze chitin resin bone flesh lattice node node2 hazard alert
//            liquid frost canvas rust rubber gold. screen, lamp, signal, resin, node, node2 and
//            liquid glow; glass is see-through; metal, chrome, bronze and gold are metallic.
// sets       name, palette (default: the set's id), level and cost (the tech-tree defaults for its
//            pieces), tab (default "deco"), selfLit (glows need no power: alien and Precursor).
// pieces     one per deco block:
//   id, name, set       the set it belongs to; "also" lists other sets it furnishes
//   roles               what it is in a room (desk, chair, bed...): templates and POI props ask for roles
//   size                footprint in small-grid cells (0.5 m): width x, height y, depth z. Its front
//                       faces -z. On the large grid it takes its size rounded up to whole 2 m cells.
//   grids               "large" (bases and capital ships, the default) and/or "small" (small vessels)
//   mount               floor (default), wall (mountY: its bottom's height), ceiling, or top (stands
//                       on a desk, table, bench or counter; those give their "surface" height)
//   walk                flat enough to step over: never blocks a walkway
//   fixed               bolted down: never knocked over. "fall" lists the ways it may fall
//                       (back, front, side, over); default all four sides
//   states              the damaged states it has (default: knocked, broken, burnt, overgrown)
//   bill                what placing it takes from shared storage (items.json ids), the same on both grids
//   level, cost         its tech-tree node (default: its set's); the first piece of a set is the set's
//                       root on the deco tab and the rest hang under it
//   light               range (m) and energy while powered; anim: flicker, blink, pulse, or spark
//                       (blinks while powered, sparks when broken)
//   palette             a piece's own palette (the alien looks)
//   uniqueOnly          needs a unique find (precursor alloy): salvage only
